 "drivingQuestion": "why and per whom is exiting meat forbidden?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "attributed to R' Yehuda ben Beteira",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "avodah_zarah.32b.5",
   "daf": "32b",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "וְהַיּוֹצֵא אָסוּר, מִפְּנֵי שֶׁהוּא כְּזִבְחֵי מֵתִים. מַאי טַעְמָא? אִי אֶפְשָׁר דְּלֵיכָּא תִּקְרוֹבֶת עֲבוֹדָה זָרָה. מַנִּי? רַבִּי יְהוּדָה בֶּן בְּתֵירָא הִיא.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «And» meat «that exits» the house of idol worship «is prohibited because it is» considered «as offerings to the dead,» i.e., idols. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» that it is classified as such? It is because it is «impossible that it is not an idolatrous offering.» The Gemara asks: «Whose» opinion does this reflect? It «is» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda ben Beteira.»"
  }
 ],
